 be added to the generated OpenAPI (e.g. visible at `/docs`).\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs for Path Operation Configuration](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/path-operation-configuration/).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='description', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Subscript(value=Name(id='Optional'), slice=Name(id='str')), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                A description for the *path operation*.\n\n                If not provided, it will be extracted automatically from the docstring\n                of the *path operation function*.\n\n                It can contain Markdown.\n\n                It will be added to the generated OpenAPI (e.g. visible at `/docs`).\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs for Path Operation Configuration](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/path-operation-configuration/).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='response_description', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Name(id='str'), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                The description for the default response.\n\n                It will be added to the generated OpenAPI (e.g. visible at `/docs`).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='responses', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Subscript(value=Name(id='Optional'), slice=Subscript(value=Name(id='Dict'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Subscript(value=Name(id='Union'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Name(id='int'), Name(id='str')])), Subscript(value=Name(id='Dict'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Name(id='str'), Name(id='Any')]))]))), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Additional responses that could be returned by this *path operation*.\n\n                It will be added to the generated OpenAPI (e.g. visible at `/docs`).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='deprecated', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Subscript(value=Name(id='Optional'), slice=Name(id='bool')), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Mark this *path operation* as deprecated.\n\n                It will be added to the generated OpenAPI (e.g. visible at `/docs`).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='operation_id', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Subscript(value=Name(id='Optional'), slice=Name(id='str')), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Custom operation ID to be used by this *path operation*.\n\n                By default, it is generated automatically.\n\n                If you provide a custom operation ID, you need to make sure it is\n                unique for the whole API.\n\n                You can customize the\n                operation ID generation with the parameter\n                `generate_unique_id_function` in the `FastAPI` class.\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs about how to Generate Clients](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/generate-clients/#custom-generate-unique-id-function).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='response_model_include', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Subscript(value=Name(id='Optional'), slice=Name(id='IncEx')), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Configuration passed to Pydantic to include only certain fields in the\n                response data.\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs for Response Model - Return Type](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/response-model/#response_model_include-and-response_model_exclude).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='response_model_exclude', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Subscript(value=Name(id='Optional'), slice=Name(id='IncEx')), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Configuration passed to Pydantic to exclude certain fields in the\n                response data.\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs for Response Model - Return Type](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/response-model/#response_model_include-and-response_model_exclude).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='response_model_by_alias', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Name(id='bool'), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Configuration passed to Pydantic to define if the response model\n                should be serialized by alias when an alias is used.\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs for Response Model - Return Type](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/response-model/#response_model_include-and-response_model_exclude).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='response_model_exclude_unset', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Name(id='bool'), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Configuration passed to Pydantic to define if the response data\n                should have all the fields, including the ones that were not set and\n                have their default values. This is different from\n                `response_model_exclude_defaults` in that if the fields are set,\n                they will be included in the response, even if the value is the same\n                as the default.\n\n                When `True`, default values are omitted from the response.\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs for Response Model - Return Type](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/response-model/#use-the-response_model_exclude_unset-parameter).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='response_model_exclude_defaults', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Name(id='bool'), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Configuration passed to Pydantic to define if the response data\n                should have all the fields, including the ones that have the same value\n                as the default. This is different from `response_model_exclude_unset`\n                in that if the fields are set but contain the same default values,\n                they will be excluded from the response.\n\n                When `True`, default values are omitted from the response.\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs for Response Model - Return Type](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/response-model/#use-the-response_model_exclude_unset-parameter).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='response_model_exclude_none', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Name(id='bool'), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Configuration passed to Pydantic to define if the response data should\n                exclude fields set to `None`.\n\n                This is much simpler (less smart) than `response_model_exclude_unset`\n                and `response_model_exclude_defaults`. You probably want to use one of\n                those two instead of this one, as those allow returning `None` values\n                when it makes sense.\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs for Response Model - Return Type](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/response-model/#response_model_exclude_none).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='include_in_schema', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Name(id='bool'), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Include this *path operation* in the generated OpenAPI schema.\n\n                This affects the generated OpenAPI (e.g. visible at `/docs`).\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs for Query Parameters and String Validations](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/query-params-str-validations/#exclude-from-openapi).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='response_class', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Subscript(value=Name(id='Type'), slice=Name(id='Response')), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Response class to be used for this *path operation*.\n\n                This will not be used if you return a response directly.\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs for Custom Response - HTML, Stream, File, others](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/custom-response/#redirectresponse).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='name', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Subscript(value=Name(id='Optional'), slice=Name(id='str')), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Name for this *path operation*. Only used internally.\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='callbacks', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Subscript(value=Name(id='Optional'), slice=Subscript(value=Name(id='List'), slice=Name(id='BaseRoute'))), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value="\n                List of *path operations* that will be used as OpenAPI callbacks.\n\n                This is only for OpenAPI documentation, the callbacks won't be used\n                directly.\n\n                It will be added to the generated OpenAPI (e.g. visible at `/docs`).\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs for OpenAPI Callbacks](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/openapi-callbacks/).\n                ")])]))), arg(arg='openapi_extra', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Subscript(value=Name(id='Optional'), slice=Subscript(value=Name(id='Dict'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Name(id='str'), Name(id='Any')]))), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Extra metadata to be included in the OpenAPI schema for this *path\n                operation*.\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs for Path Operation Advanced Configuration](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/path-operation-advanced-configuration/#custom-openapi-path-operation-schema).\n                ')])]))), arg(arg='generate_unique_id_function', annotation=Subscript(value=Name(id='Annotated'), slice=Tuple(elts=[Subscript(value=Name(id='Callable'), slice=Tuple(elts=[List(elts=[Attribute(value=Name(id='routing'), attr='APIRoute')]), Name(id='str')])), Call(func=Name(id='Doc'), args=[Constant(value='\n                Customize the function used to generate unique IDs for the *path\n                operations* shown in the generated OpenAPI.\n\n                This is particularly useful when automatically generating clients or\n                SDKs for your API.\n\n                Read more about it in the\n                [FastAPI docs about how to Generate Clients](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/generate-clients/#custom-generate-unique-id-function).\n                ')])])))], kw_defaults=[Call(func=Name(id='Default'), args=[Constant(value=None)]), Constant(value=None), Constant(value=None), Constant(value=None), Constant(value=None), Constant(value=None), Constant(value='Successful Response'), Constant(value=None), Constant(value=None), Constant(value=None), Constant(value=None), Constant(value=None), Constant(value=True), Constant(value=False), Constant(value=False), Constant(value=False), Constant(value=True), Call(func=Name(id='Default'), args=[Name(id='JSONResponse')]), Constant(value=None), Constant(value=None), Constant(value=None), Call(func=Name(id='Default'), args=[Name(id='generate_unique_id')])]), body=[Expr(value=Constant(value='\n        Add a *path operation* using an HTTP PUT operation.\n\n        ## Example\n\n        ```python\n        from fastapi import FastAPI\n        from pydantic import BaseModel\n\n        class Item(BaseModel):\n            name: str\n            description: str | None = None\n\n        app = FastAPI()\n\n        @app.put("/items/{item_id}")\n        def replace_item(item_id: str, item: Item):\n            return {"message": "Item replaced", "id": item_id}\n        ```\n        ')), Return(value=Call(func=Attribute(value=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='router'), attr='put'), args=[Name(id='path')], keywords=[keyword(arg='response_model', value=Name(id='response_model')), keyword(arg='status_code', value=Name(id='status_code')), keyword(arg='tags', value=Name(id='tags')), keyword(arg='dependencies', value=Name(id='dependencies')), keyword(arg='summary', value=Name(id='summary')), keyword(arg='description', value=Name(id='description')), keyword(arg='response_description', value=Name(id='response_description')), keyword(arg='responses', value=Name(id='responses')), keyword(arg='deprecated', value=Name(id='deprecated')), keyword(arg='operation_id', value=Name(id='operation_id')), keyword(arg='response_model_include', value=Name(id='response_model_include')), keyword(arg='response_model_exclude', value=Name(id='response_model_exclude')), keyword(arg='response_model_by_alias', value=Name(id='response_model_by_alias')), keyword(arg='response_model_exclude_unset', value=Name(id='response_model_exclude_unset')), keyword(arg='response_model_exclude_defaults', value=Name(id='response_model_exclude_defaults')), keyword(arg='response_model_exclude_none', value=Name(id='response_model_exclude_none')), keyword(arg='include_in_schema', value=Name(id='include_in_schema')), keyword(arg='response_class', value=Name(id='response_class')), keyword(arg='name', value=Name(id='name')), keyword(arg='callbacks', value=Name(id='callbacks')), keyword(arg='openapi_extra', value=Name(id='openapi_extra')), keyword(arg='generate_unique_id_function', value=Name(id='generate_unique_id_function'))]))], returns=Subscript(value=Name(id='Callable'), slice=Tuple(elts=[List(elts=[Name(